# ONT-Based DNA Methylation Analysis

**Map modification-tagged ONT reads to a T2T genome and summarize cytosine modifications in CG, CHG and CHH contexts.**

## Overview

This workflow documents the previously supplied HW64 `run.sh` commands. ONT reads are aligned to the HW64 T2T assembly using minimap2, sorted and indexed using SAMtools, and summarized using `modkit pileup`.

| Stage | Software | Main output |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Align ONT reads | minimap2 | Reference-aligned records retaining supplied modification tags |
| Sort and index alignments | SAMtools | Coordinate-sorted BAM and index |
| Aggregate modification calls | modkit | Site-level bedMethyl results for the requested contexts |

## 1. Requirements and inputs

| Requirement | Description |
| :--- | :--- |
| minimap2 | Version supporting the `lr:hq` preset and `-y` |
| SAMtools | BAM sorting and indexing |
| modkit | Version supporting the supplied `pileup` options |
| `HW64.T2T.fa` | Reference genome at the path in the script |
| `CG64_Leaf_R1.pass.fq.gz` | ONT reads, supplied as a relative path |

**Modification calls must already be present.** For this FASTQ-based workflow, the read comments must carry valid SAM-compatible modified-base tags, including MM/ML information, which minimap2 can copy to its output. Ordinary FASTQ sequence and quality strings alone do not contain methylation calls. The alignment and pileup commands do not generate those calls from raw electrical signal.

The upstream modified-base basecalling command and model were not recovered with this script. Record the model, chemistry and software versions used to produce the input reads. To analyze all three contexts, the input calls must support non-CG cytosines as well as CG cytosines; requesting additional motifs cannot create calls absent from the input.

## 2. Complete analysis code

Save the following block as `run_ONT_methylation.sh`. Run it from the directory containing `CG64_Leaf_R1.pass.fq.gz`.

The three analysis commands retain the recovered paths and parameters. A Bash header and `set -euo pipefail` have been added so that a failed alignment pipeline stops the script.

```bash
#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail

# Align modification-tagged ONT reads and sort by genomic coordinate.
minimap2 -t 60 -ax lr:hq --MD -y \
    /home/GuanJianTao/CG64.Genome.dir/Comparison.dir/assembly.dir/HW64.T2T.fa \
    CG64_Leaf_R1.pass.fq.gz \
    | samtools sort -@ 30 -o HW64.aligned.bam

# Index the sorted BAM.
samtools index -@ 60 HW64.aligned.bam

# Summarize modified-base calls in the three sequence contexts.
modkit pileup \
    HW64.aligned.bam \
    HW64.methylation_all.bed \
    --ref /home/GuanJianTao/CG64.Genome.dir/Comparison.dir/assembly.dir/HW64.T2T.fa \
    --motif CG 0 \
    --motif CHG 0 \
    --motif CHH 0 \
    --threads 60 \
    --log-filepath modkit.log
```

Run with:

```bash
bash run_ONT_methylation.sh > run_ONT_methylation.log 2>&1
```

Ensure that the reference FASTA index is available. If necessary, prepare it once before running the workflow:

```bash
samtools faidx \
    /home/GuanJianTao/CG64.Genome.dir/Comparison.dir/assembly.dir/HW64.T2T.fa
```

The FASTA indexing command is an added preparation step, rather than one of the recovered commands.

## 3. Key parameters

| Parameter | Value | Meaning |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| minimap2 `-t` | `60` | Alignment threads |
| minimap2 `-a` | Enabled | SAM output |
| minimap2 `-x` | `lr:hq` | High-accuracy long-read alignment preset |
| minimap2 `--MD` | Enabled | Include the MD alignment tag |
| minimap2 `-y` | Enabled | Copy FASTA/FASTQ comments to output; retains modification tags only when present and correctly formatted |
| SAMtools sort `-@` | `30` | Sorting compression threads |
| SAMtools index `-@` | `60` | Indexing threads |
| modkit `--ref` | HW64 T2T FASTA | Reference used for motif matching |
| modkit `--motif` | `CG 0`, `CHG 0`, `CHH 0` | Summarize the first cytosine in each motif; offsets are zero-based |
| modkit `--threads` | `60` | Pileup threads |

`H` denotes A, C or T. The three motif classes are retained together in one output file. The original command does not request strand combination or specify a fixed modified-base probability threshold; retain the modkit log and version to document the effective settings.

## 4. Main outputs

| File | Contents |
| :--- | :--- |
| `HW64.aligned.bam` | Coordinate-sorted alignments carrying the retained modification information |
| `HW64.aligned.bam.bai` | BAM index |
| `HW64.methylation_all.bed` | Extended bedMethyl table |
| `modkit.log` | modkit processing log |
| `run_ONT_methylation.log` | Combined execution log from the example launch command |

In the documented bedMethyl layout, useful fields include:

| Column | Meaning |
| :--- | :--- |
| 1–3 | Chromosome and 0-based, half-open interval |
| 4 | Modification code and motif annotation when multiple motifs are requested |
| 6 | Strand |
| 10 | Valid call coverage |
| 11 | Percent modified |
| 12 | Modified-call count |
| 13 | Canonical-call count |



